  "details": {
   "alignment": "Lawful Good",
   "deity": "",
   "size": "medium",
   "languages": "Common, Dwarvish",
   "biography": "<p><em>The Broken Anvil · Level 1 - The Recruits · Seat 1, Front line</em></p><p>A broad, red-bearded dwarf of Tenor Hold in bronze scale, round shield up and sword ready, who treats every tunnel as if it owes him money. Gruff, proud and steady as a forge-stone; he hums mining songs when nervous and polishes his shield when bored. The Broken Anvil is a Tenor forge mine, dug by his own people, and he will not hear of goblins keeping it.</p><p><strong>Tonight:</strong> This is his people&#x27;s mine, and he wants it back before the forges go cold for good.</p><h3>In a fight</h3><p>Hold the front with your shield up, so arrows struggle to reach you or the friend beside you, and hit the nearest goblin with your longsword (Advantage on the first swing each round). Trip or Intimidating Strike anything big.</p>",
   "backgroundStory": "<h3>Abilities (from the printed sheet)</h3><p><strong>Weapon Specialisation (Longsword).</strong> Advantage on the first attack roll you make with your longsword each round, and +1 damage with it (included).</p><p><strong>Combat Reflexes.</strong> Once per round, make one melee Attack of Opportunity against an enemy you can see that leaves your reach or moves past or through it. Disengage prevents it.</p><p><strong>Combat Manoeuvres.</strong> Trip, Disarm, Grapple, Dirty Trick and Push each replace one attack; Shield Blow and Guard replace all your attacks this round (Shield Blow with Disadvantage at 1st level); Cleave is an extra melee attack when you drop a foe (see Combat Manoeuvres). Your manoeuvre save DC is 13.</p><p><strong>Intimidating Strike (Fighter manoeuvre).</strong> On a hit, the target makes a Will save (DC 13) or is Frightened until the end of its next turn.</p><p><strong>Shield Wall (kit).</strong> Ranged attacks against you and an ally next to you have Disadvantage.</p><p><strong>Dwarf-Friend (kit).</strong> Advantage on dwarven clan etiquette and weapon identification checks. Dul Khagul dwarves trust you on sight; he learned the shield-wall from them.</p><p><strong>Dwarf (Tenor Hold).</strong> Speed 25ft, never reduced by armour or load. Darkvision 60ft. Advantage on stonework and underground construction checks, and on saves against poison (Resistance 5 to poison). Tenor Hold: Advantage to craft, repair or identify firearms and mechanical devices, and on checks about human cultures and languages.</p><p><strong>Stonebraced.</strong> Once per day, treat a critical hit against you as a normal hit, or ignore a knockdown.</p><p><strong>Craft: Blacksmithing.</strong> Advantage on Blacksmithing checks (the Dwarf&#x27;s free craft, not an NWP slot).</p><p><strong>The Clan Weapon.</strong> His longsword is the Brassbeard blade. If he loses it, he has Disadvantage on Charisma checks with other dwarves until it is back.</p><p><strong>Toughness (1st, General).</strong> +1 Max HP per level and +1 Constitution (both included), and Advantage on Constitution checks.</p><p><strong>Armour Class on the sheet:</strong> 10 + 4 (Scale Mail, Medium) + 1 (Dex, Medium max +2) + 1 (Shield, Medium Steel) = 16</p>"
  }
 },
 "items": [
  {
   "_id": "5DZOJ7xffeKsC3wI",
   "_key": "!actors.items!Tf5W09ItBEblxcjN.5DZOJ7xffeKsC3wI",
   "name": "Fighter",
   "type": "class",
   "img": "systems/arneyan/assets/classes/Fighter.webp",
   "system": {
    "description": "<table class=\"arn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Trait</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Key Attribute</td><td>Strength / Dexterity</td></tr><tr><td>Hit Die</td><td><strong>d10</strong></td></tr><tr><td>HP beyond 10th</td><td>+<strong>3 HP</strong> a level, plus your Constitution modifier</td></tr><tr><td>BtH</td><td>+2 per 3 levels (+8 at 12th, +16 at 24th)</td></tr><tr><td>Complexity</td><td>★★☆☆☆ Easy</td></tr><tr><td>Weapons</td><td>Any</td></tr><tr><td>Armour</td><td>Any armour and shields.</td></tr><tr><td>Kit</td><td>At character creation choose a Kit: your fighting tradition and where you learned it (see Kits).</td></tr><tr><td>Identity</td><td>Master of the fundamentals: any weapon, any armour, and combat manoeuvres no one else can match. Where other classes lean on tricks, the Fighter wins by doing the basics better than anyone.</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Level by Level at a Glance</h2><p><em>What you gain and when. Full details are under Class Abilities.</em></p><table class=\"arn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Lvl</th><th>You gain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Weapon Specialisation, Combat Manoeuvres, Combat Reflexes</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Manoeuvre Mastery</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Battle Space</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Combat Dominance</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Unbroken</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Legend of Battle</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Extra Attack, Weapon Specialisation +2</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Combat Dominance (3 attacks), Shield Mastery</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Manoeuvre Mastery improves</td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Combat Dominance (4 attacks)</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>Battle Space improves, second Weapon Specialisation</td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>+1 Strength</td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Battle Space improves</td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Manoeuvre Mastery improves, Weapon Specialisation +3, +1 Strength or Dexterity</td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>Legend of Battle improves</td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>Battle Space (Master)</td></tr><tr><td>24</td><td>Unbroken improves</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Class Abilities</h2><h3 class=\"arn-level\">1st Level</h3><ul><li><strong>Weapon Specialisation:</strong> Choose one weapon — you have <strong>Advantage</strong> on the first attack roll you make with it each round, and gain +1 damage with it.</li><li>Improves to +2 damage at 7th level</li><li>Improves to +3 damage at 19th level</li><li>At 13th level, choose a second weapon to specialise in, or add a further +1 damage to your first</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">1st Level — Combat Manoeuvres</h3><ul><li><strong>Combat Manoeuvres:</strong> Every character can use every manoeuvre; the Fighter's edge is Manoeuvre Mastery. See the Combat Manoeuvres section for details.</li><li><strong>Combat Reflexes:</strong> You have the Combat Reflexes feat for free (see The Feats of Arneyan in Character Creation). It doesn't use a feat slot.</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">2nd Level — Manoeuvre Mastery</h3><ul><li><strong>Manoeuvre Mastery:</strong> Manoeuvres that impose disadvantage on your own attack roll (Shield Blow) are now rolled normally, with no disadvantage.</li><li>9th level: Contest-based manoeuvres (Trip, Disarm, Dirty Trick) are now rolled with advantage.</li><li>19th level: Manoeuvres that previously imposed disadvantage on your attack roll are now rolled with advantage instead.</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">3rd Level — Battle Space</h3><ul><li><strong>Battle Space:</strong> You control the space around you in ways most fighters never learn.</li><li>You count as flanking a creature whenever an ally is also in melee with it, not only when directly opposite</li><li>13th level: +1 AC unless wielding a two-handed weapon, and you reroll 1s on Flank Attack damage</li><li>17th level: a Flank Attack also deals +1 damage die</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">4th Level — Combat Dominance</h3><ul><li><strong>Combat Dominance:</strong> When every creature you attack this round is of Level up to half your character Level, you can make extra attacks (your Fighter level sets how many, below), split among them as you like.</li><li>4th level: 2 attacks per round against creatures of Level up to half your character Level</li><li>8th level: 3 attacks per round against creatures of Level up to half your character Level</li><li>12th level: 4 attacks per round against creatures of Level up to half your character Level</li><li>All but the first attack are rolled with <strong>Disadvantage</strong>. Combat Dominance replaces the Extra Attack and the off-hand attack; Flowing Strikes can still add one.</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">5th Level — Unbroken</h3><ul><li><strong>Unbroken:</strong> Once per day, when reduced to <strong>0 HP</strong> or below, immediately stand at <strong>1 HP</strong>.</li><li>No save, no check — pure will</li><li>24th level: once per encounter instead; for the next round you are immune to all damage and your attacks deal +2 damage dice, then normal rules resume</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">6th Level — Legend of Battle</h3><ul><li><strong>Legend of Battle:</strong> Once per day, for <strong>1 round</strong> you become a force of war that lesser fighters can only dream of.</li><li>All attack rolls are made with advantage</li><li>Every hit deals maximum damage — no rolling</li><li>20th level: lasts <strong>1 minute</strong>, and enemies that can see you must make a <strong>Will save</strong> (Class Save DC) at the start of each of their turns or be frightened for <strong>1 round</strong></li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">7th Level — Extra Attack</h3><ul><li><strong>Extra Attack:</strong> When you use your action to attack, make one additional weapon attack as part of it, with <strong>Disadvantage</strong> (see Extra attacks in The Arneyan Codex).</li><li>Does not stack with Combat Dominance — choose one or the other each round</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">8th Level — Shield Mastery</h3><ul><li><strong>Shield Mastery:</strong> Use a shield as a second weapon without the normal two-weapon attack penalty. It is a Light weapon dealing <strong>1d4</strong> (<strong>1d6</strong> for a Tower Shield), and it keeps its AC bonus.</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">15th Level — Strength Bonus</h3><ul><li><strong>Strength Bonus:</strong> Gain a permanent +1 to Strength.</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">19th Level — Attribute Bonus</h3><ul><li><strong>Attribute Bonus:</strong> Gain a permanent +1 to either Strength or Dexterity.</li></ul><h3 class=\"arn-level\">22nd Level — Battle Space (Master)</h3><ul><li><strong>Battle Space</strong> (Master): You move through combat like water — nothing holds you and nothing catches you.</li><li>When you attack, you may also Disengage from any number of enemies as part of the same action</li><li>You have <strong>Advantage</strong> on <strong>Reflex saves</strong></li><li>A Flank Attack deals +2 damage dice instead, and the target cannot make Attacks of Opportunity against you until the start of your next turn</li></ul><h2>Combat Manoeuvres</h2><p>Every manoeuvre in the Combat Manoeuvres section is available to the Fighter from 1st level, and Mastery tiers unlock at 2nd, 9th and 19th level (see Class Abilities). The Fighter also has one manoeuvre of their own:</p><table class=\"arn-table\"><thead><tr><th>Manoeuvre</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Intimidating Strike</td><td>On a hit, target makes <strong>Will save</strong> or is frightened until end of its next turn</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Kits</h2><p class=\"arn-note\">Each kit is an item in the <strong>Kits</strong> compendium, in the Fighter folder. Drag one onto your character.</p><p>Choose one Kit at character creation. Kits represent your fighting tradition, background, and the culture that forged you.</p>",
